<title>FRANCE: France's Lamassoure optimistic on stability pact.</title>
<headline>France's Lamassoure optimistic on stability pact.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French government spokesman Alain Lamassoure said on Wednesday he was optimistic a compromise deal would be found on a stability pact to impose budgetary discipline on members of a future single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;We are heading toward a compromise,&quot; he told Europe 1 radio.</p>
<p>Germany has been isolated in seeking limits on budget deficits with automatic fines for violations except in numerically defined exceptional circumstances.</p>
<p>&quot;We want something that is rigorous but more supple to take into national sovereignty and to ensure that budgetary and fiscal policy remains under the authority of national parliaments,&quot; Lamassoure said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
